# item_acquisition — the outcome, not the verb.
#
# cli/verb/gather/ proves the verb prints "Item received:". This proves the chip corresponds to
# something real: the item is in the pack afterwards and was not there before. The two overlap on
# purpose — same scenario, different question.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Berry Bush"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# --- before: the pack does not hold what the bush has ---------------------------
inspect items
expect-no-state items hawthorn_berry

strategy succeed
goal gather
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# --- the chip, and that it was this outcome that ran -----------------------------
expect Item received:
expect-outcome item_acquisition

# --- after: it is really carried -------------------------------------------------
# The point of the whole range. A verb whose SuccessReports built the chip and never reached the
# pack would satisfy every assertion above this line.
inspect items
expect-state items hawthorn_berry
quit
